{title: Tell Me the Old, Old Story}
{title_ko: 주 예수 크신 사랑}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 205장}
{artist: Katherine Hankey / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{key_original: C}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Tell me the old, old story of un[C7]seen things a[F]bove
Of Jesus and His glory, of [Bb]Jesus and His [F]love
Tell me the story simply, as to a [C7]little [F]child
For I am weak and weary, and [Bb]helpless and de[F]filed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Tell me the old, old story,
Tell me the old, old story,
[C7]Tell me the old, old story
Of [F]Jesus and His love
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Tell me the story slowly, that I may [C7]take it [F]in
That wonderful re[Bb]demption, God's [F]remedy for sin
Tell me the story often, for I for[C7]get so [F]soon
The early dew of morning has [Bb]passed a[F]way at noon
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
